Companion to fuse2fs-mkfs-and-fsck.patch: _mkfs_dev is the mkfs entry
point for extra devices (dm targets: thin volumes, error targets). With
"do nothing for fuse" the dm-thin tests mount a device that never got a
filesystem — generic/347's post-test e2fsck then finds no superblock at
all. Same fuse2fs-can-really-mkfs rationale as the scratch/test hunks.

--- a/common/rc
+++ b/common/rc
@@ -906,7 +906,9 @@ _try_mkfs_dev()
 	# do nothing for 9p
 	;;
     fuse)
-	# do nothing for fuse
+	if [ "$FUSE_SUBTYP" = ".fuse2fs" ]; then
+		mkfs.ext4 -Fq -O ^has_journal $* >/dev/null 2>&1
+	fi
 	;;
     virtiofs)
 	# do nothing for virtiofs
